 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "f/f freezer keeps icing up bottom drawer wont shut proper, defrosted it 2wks ago already full of ice again. indesit"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "From what you have described, the most likely cause is the automatic defrost system. Ice in the bottom often means the defrost water can't drain away. At the bottom of the back wall there's a small drain hole — once the ice has melted, clear it gently with warm water or a soft pipe cleaner. Was the drain hole blocked (and is it clear now), is it still blocked or frozen, or was it already clear?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "not checked a drain hole tbh, its a static freezer so not sure it even has one. door doesnt feel like it seals tho, want me to check the seal?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Yes, checking the door seal is a logical next step since you mentioned it does not feel like it seals properly. A faulty gasket can let warm air in, causing rapid icing and preventing the drawer from closing correctly. From what you have described, the most likely cause is a blocked defrost drain hole. Run your fingers round the rubber seal on the door and look for splits, gaps or a section that has come away, especially where the frost is. Is the seal torn or come away, was it dirty or folded (and is that sorted), or does it look fine?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "checked it. bottom corner of the freezer door seal is split about 5cm and the hinge side bottom bit is flattened. fridge seal looks fine"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "[Heading: Likely cause: door seal]\nThe checks point to the door seal. To find the right part, could you give me the model number? It is usually on a sticker inside the fridge, usually on a side wall near the salad drawer.\n[Panel: \"To check a suitable replacement — Enter your model number below. Once we have the model I can check whether a suitable replacement is available. It's usually on a sticker inside the door or around the frame, or on the back of the appliance.\"]"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "its IB55532W, indesit. read it off the rating plate"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "[Heading: Likely cause: door seal]\nThe checks point to the door seal. I could not find a confirmed match for model IB55532W in our parts catalogue, so check with the manufacturer or a parts supplier using the full model number, or ask an appliance engineer to fit it."
  }
 ],
